DeviceType.description:
Discriminates the kind of device. `bigip` (default) is a BIG-IP device;
`f5os` is an F5OS platform provider (e.g. rSeries). When omitted the
device is treated as a BIG-IP for backward compatibility.

detail.description:
Structured extra data relevant to the check result.
Examples:
  disk_space:           { available_gb: 8.2, threshold_gb: 15.0 }
  cluster:              { healthy_nodes: 1, install_done: 2, install_total: 2 }
  cores:                { count: 2, files: ["core.123", "core.456"] }
  fpga_status:          { has_fpga: true, ready_nodes: 1, total_nodes: 1 }
  tenant_status:        { blocking_tenants: ["tenant-a: running-state=\"deployed\" status=\"Pending\""] }
  upgrade_path:         { current_version: "15.1.2", target_version: "17.1.5", min_source_version: "16.1.0" }
  license_date:         { license_check_date: "2024-01-15", service_check_date: "2023-12-01" }
